## 3. Managing Issues & Pull Requests

Create, manage, and track work directly from Slack without switching contexts.

### Essential Slash Commands

| Command | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- |
| `/github open OWNER/REPO` | Prompts you to create a new issue with a title and description. |
| `/github close [ISSUE-LINK]` | Closes the specified issue. Add `reason:"NOT-PLANNED"` to specify a reason. |
| `/github reopen [ISSUE-LINK]` | Reopens a closed issue. |
| `/github signin` / `/github signout` | Connect or disconnect your GitHub account from Slack. |
| `/github settings` | Open the interactive menu to configure threading, default repos, and preferences. |

### Smart Mentions
Once your accounts are linked, GitHub will automatically `@mention` you in Slack when:
- You are assigned to an issue or PR.
- Your review is requested on a PR or deployment.
- You are `@mentioned` in a GitHub comment, issue, or discussion.
*(Note: Mentions only work in the Slack workspace where you most recently logged into the GitHub app).*

